## PART 3: AWS AIF-C01 Tool — Implementation Reference

### File location
`~/Documents/AWS_Learning/aws_aif/AWS_AIF_C01_Learning_Tool.html`

### Specs
- **153 questions**: 133 MCQ, 12 multi-select, 8 true/false
- **Difficulty**: 47 Easy, 101 Medium, 5 Hard
- **Size**: ~220 KB, ~1230 lines
- **5 iterations × 5 rounds × 13 questions** = 65 per iteration
- **Pass score**: 70%
- **Header badge**: shows "153 Q" (total question count)
- **Question types**: "mcq" (single-select), "msq" (multi-select), "order" (ordering/HOTSPOT with up/down reorder arrows)
- **Review Wrong Answers**: Button in iteration results shows all wrong Qs with user answer, correct answer, and detailed "why wrong" explanation

### Learning Mode sections (15 total across 5 domains)
| Domain | Sections |
|--------|----------|
| AI/ML Fundamentals (20%) | AI/ML Basics, ML Evaluation Metrics, Overfitting/Drift, SageMaker & MLOps, AWS AI Services |
| Generative AI (24%) | GenAI & FMs, Prompt Engineering, Multimodal, Cost Concepts, RLHF & DPO |
| Foundation Models (28%) | Bedrock, Agents & Knowledge Bases, Guardrails, Optimizing Inference |
| Responsible AI (14%) | Principles, Bias Detection & Mitigation |
| Security & Governance (14%) | Threats/Protections, Governance |

### DOMAIN_ALIASES (for results breakdown)
Questions use service-level domain names. Map to official exam domains:
- `AWS Managed AI Services`, `Amazon SageMaker`, `Bedrock & Generative AI`
  → `Applications of Foundation Models`
- `Prompt Engineering` → `Fundamentals of Generative AI`
- `AI Challenges & Responsibilities` → `Guidelines for Responsible AI`
- `AWS Security Services` → `Security, Compliance, and Governance for AI`

### Question sources
1. masteryexamprep.com (original 60 questions — URLs now 404)
2. Ditectrev/AIF-C01 GitHub repo (~35 additional questions)
3. techexamlexicon.com, study4exam.com (supplementary)
4. open-exam-prep.com (8 questions — SageMaker, RAG, Bedrock, FM concepts)
5. javainuse.com (41 questions reviewed, 0 added — already covered by existing)
6. devpath.com (22 questions — ML lifecycle, GenAI, prompt eng, responsible AI, security)
7. free-braindumps.com (56 questions extracted from pages 1-8 of 43; 22 unique added — PDPs, Amazon Q, SageMaker Serverless, Bedrock pricing, GenAI Security Scoping Matrix, Guardrails, GAN, plagiarism, model evaluation)

### Key decisions
- Shuffle once per iteration (LCG PRNG), contiguous round slices + wrap-around
- No comma separation for "Select TWO" multi-select in UI
- Domain aliases to normalize non-standard domain names in results
- Pass score 70% (exam standard)
- Clean up scraped/ temp files after adding questions (don't commit to git)

